## Goal
Fix a race in the Ask panel (DEV-47): if a link is dispatched to the panel after application termination has started, it must not wait on a panel that termination never cancels.

## Problems
A cross-review (Codex) flagged that a panel dispatch can race with app termination. An in-flight ask keeps waiting on a panel termination did not cancel, so the app's timeout may terminate before the link is opened. The race depends on Objective-C main-queue ordering, so Go tests cannot reproduce it. The review tooling also failed once and had to be rerun.

## Decision
In `internal/handler/panel.m`, asks dispatched after termination has begun now resolve straight to the default answer without showing a panel. This closes the window where termination misses a late-dispatched ask. Verification is limited to `make test` and the cgo build, which confirm compilation.

